# Copy to .env.local and fill with your own values if you need to
# override the shared defaults in .env:
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# .env (tracked) holds the shared public defaults so `npm run dev` works
# out of the box. .env.local (gitignored) wins when present.

# Public Supabase project URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co

# Public publishable key (safe for the browser)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=sb_publishable_your_key_here

# Server-only secrets below — NEVER commit real values.
# Put these in .env.local only:

# Required. Onboarding and every domain write run through the service-role
# client in utils/supabase/admin.ts, because the baseline RLS policies define
# SELECT rules only: a publishable key cannot insert a umkms, influencers or
# profiles row, and there is no per-user write policy to fall back on yet.
# Local default lives in .env; find a remote one with:
#   npx supabase projects api-keys --project-ref <ref> --reveal
# `--reveal` is required — without it the secret comes back masked. Do not paste
# the result into chat or commit it.
# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=sb_secret_your_service_role_key_here

# Notes
# -----
# - Demo one-click sign-in reads NODE_ENV, not a variable: it is refused in a
#   production build outright, so there is nothing to configure or to leak.
# - Sign-up auto-confirms the address only when NODE_ENV !== "production".
#   The local stack sets enable_confirmations = false, so both paths are open
#   in development and the stricter one is the production default.
# - `npx supabase db reset` seeds Postgres from supabase/seed.sql. `npm run
#   db:seed` seeds SQLite from lib/seed.ts. Postgres is the app's only store now;
#   the SQLite mirror is kept only so the SQLite↔Postgres verification scripts
#   stay runnable, and nothing in the app reads it.